ue":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T06:11:26-08:00","id":388371,"title":"","content":"Poor Boot. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Loving the Dinosaur. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-01T13:11:53-08:00","id":388795,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/311220-god-kicking-boot-an-exalted-comic-by-wise-old-guru?p=388371#post388371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Poor Boot. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Loving the Dinosaur. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed on both counts. Poor Boot. I was afraid of that...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T08:19:37-08:00","id":398781,"title":"","content":"So, the question is, is this suspected lunar going to just screw up the sacrifice and have the village piss off the Rain God? Or just kill Boot's father/everyone?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T12:42:21-08:00","id":399188,"title":"","content":"Look at what Boot's holding... I don't think the Lunar is going to have a chance to be the one to screw things up...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-09T13:41:32-08:00","id":399237,"title":"","content":"That elephant is cool as shit. I'll miss him after the flashback.<br /> <br /> It's hard to tell the intention of the Lunar from what we currently know. Clearly, there is an agenda at play, but I think there is more to the plan than messing up a rain festival. Chinwe was a Nellens; maybe the Lunar wants to infiltrate that house through an angle that Chinwe could provide? In any case, I think the rain festival thing is coincidental. As is Boot, for that matter. I like imagining that this is one of those &quot;for you it was the most important day of your life, but for me it was Tuesday&quot; kind of things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T05:10:42-08:00","id":406597,"title":"","content":"Oh, boy. There's no speed lines so I didn't notice it at first. There's no sneaking about, Boot is getting straight to the point. I wonder how <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/comics/2087220/page-22-ceremony-shattering-shout/\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> is going to turn out?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T06:27:58-08:00","id":406615,"title":"","content":"I'm guessing that it is going to be Princess Snout's lucky day. Everyone else... no so much....","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T16:59:56-08:00","id":407142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Greyman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/311220-god-kicking-boot-an-exalted-comic-by-wise-old-guru?p=406597#post406597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, boy. There's no speed lines so I didn't notice it at first. There's no sneaking about, Boot is getting straight to the point. I wonder how <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/comics/2087220/page-22-ceremony-shattering-shout/\" target=\"_blank\">this</a> is going to turn out?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not really a huge fan of speed lines? I'll probably use them when there's Essence effects going on, because glowing objects moving quickly create afterimages and the like. I'll try to lay out the page in such a way that it draws the eye to the action without them, and I'll be trying a few other tricks (like the one in next week's strip) to illustrate motion without relying on them. We'll see how it works out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-15T19:59:03-08:00","id":407292,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/311220-god-kicking-boot-an-exalted-comic-by-wise-old-guru?p=407142#post407142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not really a huge fan of speed lines? I'll probably use them when there's Essence effects going on, because glowing objects moving quickly create afterimages and the like. I'll try to lay out the page in such a way that it draws the eye to the action without them, and I'll be trying a few other tricks (like the one in next week's strip) to illustrate motion without relying on them. We'll see how it works out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, the big golden knife hovering in the middle of the right of the page <i>is</i> kind of obvious once you notice it. It just somehow took me a few moments to connect it with Boot's stance.<br /> <br /> I guess I'm just used to motion guides. I'll watch out for that.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T21:06:56-08:00","id":417154,"title":"","content":"Ah, yeah, I missed the dagger too. I thought she was just pointing accusingly. Speedlines or not, the movement needed to be visualised somehow.<br /> <br /> We know that Chinwe was a Nellens and so have gotten basic Dynastic training, so it's not entirely strange that she might be able to catch a dagger midflight despite not being an Exalt, so that might not be reason for suspicion in the Governor's eyes. Still, a bit surprised that he was so easily stabbed. He's a Terrestrial from what I understand, so one might have expected some sort of surprise negator? Then again, he does seem a bit naive, so maybe this will be a lesson to him. If he survives the night, that is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 02-24-2015, 05:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-23T21:54:25-08:00","id":417193,"title":"","content":"Maybe the governor favored resistance instead of dodge?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T01:04:18-08:00","id":417331,"title":"","content":"oh dear, this imposter seems to be enjoying teaching the &quot;art of stabbing everything with sharp and/or pointy objects&quot; i may be inclined to believe that this is no lunar at all... then again there is nothing that says lunars can't be terrible people to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T02:50:48-08:00","id":417384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/311220-god-kicking-boot-an-exalted-comic-by-wise-old-guru?p=417193#post417193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe the governor favored resistance instead of dodge?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's blood coming out there, though. Pretty heavy flow, and that's after the blade went through armour. Maybe he's just not a big combatant. The sword and armour might be mostly ceremonial.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/311220-god-kicking-boot-an-exalted-comic-by-wise-old-guru?p=417331#post417331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">oh dear, this imposter seems to be enjoying teaching the &quot;art of stabbing everything with sharp and/or pointy objects&quot; i may be inclined to believe that this is no lunar at all... then again there is nothing that says lunars can't be terrible people to.</div> </div> </div> </div>A big part of Lunar power acquisition amounts to killing stuff and drinking its blood. I'm not sure why you'd think a Lunar resorting to underhanded violence is implausible. Not saying it can't be something else, but right now, all the signs are awfully indicative of Lunarhood.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 02-24-2015, 05:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T03:18:48-08:00","id":417396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/311220-god-kicking-boot-an-exalted-comic-by-wise-old-guru?p=417384#post417384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's blood coming out there, though. Pretty heavy flow, and that's after the blade went through armour. Maybe he's just not a big combatant. The sword and armour might be mostly ceremonial.<br /> <br /> A big part of Lunar power acquisition amounts to killing stuff and drinking its blood. I'm not sure why you'd think a Lunar resorting to underhanded violence is implausible. Not saying it can't be something else, but right now, all the signs are awfully indicative of Lunarhood.</div> </div> </div> </div>that i know but it's more the part that she seems to enjoy murdering people in front of a child whilst wearing said child's mothers form. that i feel is a bit well i guess psychopathic/sadistic, i mean you don't traumatize the family of the prey that you sacred hunt if you've managed to hunt sneakily already. also i just noticed there doesn't seem to be much blood on her mothers corpse, one would think having ones heart torn out and eaten would cause a bit more blood...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T10:59:26-08:00","id":417694,"title":"","content":"Just because you were Exalted by Luna doesn't mean you are good person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-24T13:50:48-08:00","id":417929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/311220-god-kicking-boot-an-exalted-comic-by-wise-old-guru?p=417694#post417694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because you were Exalted by Luna doesn't mean you are good person.</div> </div> </div> </div>aye that i know","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-27T03:21:56-08:00","id":421547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/311220-god-kicking-boot-an-exalted-comic-by-wise-old-guru?p=417396#post417396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">that i know but it's more the part that she seems to enjoy murdering people in front of a child whilst wearing said child's mothers form. that i feel is a bit well i guess psychopathic/sadistic, i mean you don't traumatize the family of the prey that you sacred hunt if you've managed to hunt sneakily already.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, but the big clue that you <i>haven't</i> managed it, is said child throwing a dagger at your face.<br /> <br /> When your cover is blown, then it is time for plan B: maximum shock and awe, before beating a hasty retreat amid the ensuing chaos.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xanroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/311220-god-kicking-boot-an-exalted-comic-by-wise-old-guru?p=417396#post417396\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">also i just noticed there doesn't seem to be much blood on her mothers corpse, one would think having ones heart torn out and eaten would cause a bit more blood...</div> </div> </div> </div>If posing as a relative while having tea qualifies* as a sacred <i>hunt</i> then too &quot;Heart's Blood&quot; doesn't <i>have</i> to be <i>that </i>literal, either. As long as the metaphorical conditions are satisfied you don't <i>have</i> to make a mess on the carpet.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">* sure, and why not?</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":487,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","user":"Greyman","date":". 02-27-2015, 06:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/487-greyman","name":"Greyman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar487_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T11:10:00-08:00","id":424314,"title":"","content":"I like that the governor figured out what is up before the father. Too bad, the governor resorted to Melee instead of Martial Arts or something.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T18:33:55-08:00","id":424736,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/311220-god-kicking-boot-an-exalted-comic-by-wise-old-guru?p=417694#post417694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just because you were Exalted by Luna doesn't mean you are good person.</div> </div> </div> </div>Too early to say we're dealing with a Lunar here. An Abyssal or Sidereal could do more or less all of what this person is doing quite well.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh wait, &quot;First Dexterity Excellency&quot;, Never mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:orangered\">Duly Elected Guild Hierarch</span> of the Exalted Forum<br /> <a href=\"http://northernfoxgames.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://northernfoxgames.com/</a></b>","edited":{"userid":331,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","user":"The Revenge of TV Head","date":". 03-01-2015, 09:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/331-the-revenge-of-tv-head","name":"The Revenge of TV Head","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar331_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1272"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-01T19:58:51-08:00","id":424792,"title":"","content":"In this page, the movement is much more apparent even without movement lines. I think the throw from the earlier page could have worked if there had been a frame showing Boot pulling it back for a throw, and if the knife had been more visible in the page, like maybe a bit more centered or with a visible gleam or something.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh, yeah, and it's also a great page. I like that the Governor caught on quick at least. Not!Chinwe got sweet moves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 03-01-2015, 11:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T00:51:31-08:00","id":424960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/311220-god-kicking-boot-an-exalted-comic-by-wise-old-guru?p=424792#post424792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this page, the movement is much more apparent even without movement lines. I think the throw from the earlier page could have worked if there had been a frame showing Boot pulling it back for a throw, and if the knife had been more visible in the page, like maybe a bit more centered or with a visible gleam or something.<br /> <br /> Edit: Oh, yeah, and it's also a great page. I like that the Governor caught on quick at least. Not!Chinwe got sweet moves.</div> </div> </div> </div>The ceremonial blue ribbons here are acting as motion lines would, as sort of contrails behind the motions involved. I think it came out okay, but I'm still considering how best to depict motion without using standard comic motion lines. I'll be toying with a few ideas over the next few months, which will be a bit more kung-fu heavy than the story has been so far.<br /> <br /> Anyway, thanks for the ongoing commentary. It's really rewarding and encouraging to see people speculating about an ongoing story you're making.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T05:44:02-08:00","id":425040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/311220-god-kicking-boot-an-exalted-comic-by-wise-old-guru?p=424960#post424960\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The ceremonial blue ribbons here are acting as motion lines would, as sort of contrails behind the motions involved. I think it came out okay, but I'm still considering how best to depict motion without using standard comic motion lines. I'll be toying with a few ideas over the next few months, which will be a bit more kung-fu heavy than the story has been so far.<br /> <br /> Anyway, thanks for the ongoing commentary. It's really rewarding and encouraging to see people speculating about an ongoing story you're making.</div> </div> </div> </div>like Weimann said, great page guru. awesome work with the shadows on the wall you did awesome with the shadows &quot;bending&quot; to &quot;fit&quot; the statue (don't know exactly to describe it i hope i make sene). <br /> some small tips i can give about depicting motion is to pretty much incorporate the moving characters hair, clothes (like you did with the ribbons) or other things into the motion, this is one of the reasons why most of my characters have been drawn with relatively long hair or with somewhat loose/flowing clothes (actually you more or less used all of the examples i gave in this page so this might have been a bit redundant as a tip <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />).<br /> another tip depending on the style you want to go for (this type of motion drawing is usually seen in anime and manga) you could exaggerate some the movement, example character A throws an object then you can potentially exaggerate the movement by having character A's arm have an almost whip like transition from &quot;arm backwards&quot; to &quot;arm forwards&quot;.<br /> I hope i make sense and that those tips are of some use, and like i mentioned fantastic page keep up the good work","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T10:45:57-08:00","id":425419,"title":"","content":"Hey, sharing suggestions and tips among artists never hurts and can sometimes help, so don't worry about being redundant.<br /> <br /> I had thought about blur-lines or a slightly more cartoony distortion for motion effects, and I may play with those later. Thanks!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-02T15:27:39-08:00","id":425728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/311220-god-kicking-boot-an-exalted-comic-by-wise-old-guru?p=425419#post425419\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, sharing suggestions and tips among artists never hurts and can sometimes help, so don't worry about being redundant.<br /> <br /> I had thought about blur-lines or a slightly more cartoony distortion for motion effects, and I may play with those later. Thanks!</div> </div> </div> </div>oh i just remembered a couple of things that might help just in general, smudge tool is godlike for certain effects like movement and fire it can be difficult to use sometimes though since it's easy to over use it sometimes, also desaturation is fantastic for when you want something to be less well attention grabbing (it's the best way to describe it) i personally use it a lot for my backgrounds to make it seem farther away than it actually is and causes the none desaturated parts to pop out from the background","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T09:17:54-07:00","id":432629,"title":"","content":"Yes! Kick that Anathema's ass, Governor! <br /> <br /> And Boot, don't tell the Anathema what you (or your elephant) are going to do next. They got enough advantages as it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T10:08:54-07:00","id":432704,"title":"","content":"This page reminded me way too much about <a href=\"http://i.imgur.com/bKkeeDG.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">this</a>. I am awful.<br /> <br /> But hell yeah, Mongkut! Even a Lunar will have to take that much oncoming momentum into account. Something happened to its back, it seems, so it'll have to pull some trickery to get out of this one. Shifting doesn't mend injuries, correct? It can't shift into a healthy shape and get out?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/311220-god-kicking-boot-an-exalted-comic-by-wise-old-guru?p=432629#post432629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes! Kick that Anathema's ass, Governor!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I feel he's coming in nicely. I'm almost a bit ashamed I thought he'd get get one-shotted from a surprise attack. I need to have more faith in the author.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/311220-god-kicking-boot-an-exalted-comic-by-wise-old-guru?p=432629#post432629\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And Boot, don't tell the Anathema what you (or your elephant) are going to do next. They got enough advantages as it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Clearly Boot has gained metafictional knowledge and knows about stunting. She will Exalt as a Sidereal shortly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":75,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","user":"Weimann","date":". 03-08-2015, 01:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T10:41:02-07:00","id":432727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Weimann</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/311220-god-kicking-boot-an-exalted-comic-by-wise-old-guru?p=432704#post432704\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I feel he's coming in nicely. I'm almost a bit ashamed I thought he'd get get one-shotted from a surprise attack. I need to have more faith in the author.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Governor's preferred pronoun is &quot;she,&quot; actually. She's a bit androgynous, I know<i>, </i>but she'd be quite insulted if you mistook her for a man. Matriarchal society and all that.<br /> <br /> People refer to her as Governess when discussing her in third person, but people talking to face call her Governor. I honestly didn't notice that I was doing that when I was writing it...but I'm just gonna claim it's an in-universe language translation thing, or an An-Teng &quot;I am referred to as both male and female, for I rule over the public sphere and the private sphere, and am linked both to politics and the spirit of the land&quot; thing, since I've done it a couple times now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":512,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","user":"Wise Old Guru","date":". 03-08-2015, 01:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T06:40:34-07:00","id":442467,"title":"","content":"Victorious Mongkut is best elephant. Really love that frame.<br /> <br /> Two things. Mongkut now has a snake-like thing around his leg, and I can clearly see two huge horns protruding from the wrecked mess, none of which are Mongkut's broken tusk. I'm inclined to believe phase two is about to start. That said, I'm still curious as to if the broken back is healed, or if it has a form that somehow works around that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Dex Davican wrote:</b> I can say without exaggeration or dishonesty that I am the most creative man <i>ever to have lived</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/75-weimann","name":"Weimann","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar75_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1279"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T07:50:09-07:00","id":442516,"title":"","content":"I think the lunar has horns now too. <br /> <br /> I'm rather worried that Mongkut isn't going to survive the fight. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T10:19:54-07:00","id":442763,"title":"","content":"Like Guru said on the comic page,a little thing like that isn't gonna keep a Lunar down for long... hit it again, Mongkut!<br /> <br /> In other news, the comic's title really would be an excellent name for a Lunar (TAW?), Abyssal, or Isidoros charm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1419-wardragon","name":"WarDragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1419_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1052"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T10:22:30-07:00","id":442764,"title":"","content":"The Lunar came for revenge, and was surprised that Chinwe (the Lunar's target) had borne and raised a child. Though the pretext of getting Chinwe out of retirement was false, I think the Lunar was telling the truth when he said that Boot's existence threw his old plans off, because he told Chinwe that he had given up on revenge and now merely wanted to understand what she had done in Denzik that even she thought she deserved to die for.<br /> <br /> Either the Lunar was sufficiently enraged by the answers to change his mind again about wanting revenge, or Chinwe learned something about the Lunar's plans that made her risk fighting an Anathema alone. They fought, and Chinwe went down surprisingly hard for a mortal given the damage to the room, and then the Lunar took her face, stuffed her into the closet, and waited for the family to return.<br /> <br /> The Lunar has some ability to mimic the persona of the person whose face she wears; enough to know how to sound like Chinwe enough that her husband, daughter and governess don't suspect anything until she stabs the governess, despite limited time getting to know Chinwe. But if the Lunar is tapping into memories (such as for all those House of Bells stories of Boot's mother), it's obviously imperfect, as he didn't know the secret name that Chinwe demanded of him.<br /> <br /> Well, the Lunar's imitation also slipped up in regards to behavior towards children, which is what tipped Chinwe off. Either the Lunar's mimicry is based on observation and he didn't know that about his victim, or else the surprise of Boot's existence provoked the Lunar to act genuinely towards the child without even realizing that he had broken character.<br /> <br /> In any case, the Lunar sets out with husband and daughter to perform the rain goddess' ritual, with a Dragon-Blooded governor within arm's distance. Perhaps the Lunar was waiting for the festival to start and everyone to let their guards down before she lured the Terrestrial to a secluded spot and murdered her. (Directly attacking the governess any other day of the year probably means she's surrounded by guards and people who are paying attention to her, so stealthy murder is much harder.)<br /> <br /> However, after the Lunar's cover is blown, she only attacks the Terrestrial once to weaken her, and then spreads her attention around. Even if mortals are a greater danger to Exalted than in previous Editions, if the Lunar was there specifically to kill the governess, it would make more sense to &quot;focus-fire&quot; on the only other Exalted around until she is dead, and then run away.<br /> <br /> Since the Lunar did NOT laser-focus on the Terrestrial, I have to assume there's some other purpose for her being there at the festival.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 03-15-2015, 01:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T11:13:52-07:00","id":442834,"title":"","content":"Ah, how I wish my players looked at mysteries with the eyes you use!<br /> <br /> Storytelling murder mysteries would be much more satisfying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>So I'm making <a href=\"http://godkickingboot.smackjeeves.com/\" target=\"_blank\">God-Kicking Boot</a>, an Exalted webcomic, now. Updates on Sundays. Full-color, mediocre but slowly improving art. It's a thing.<br /> <br /> The absence of a monument can, in its own way, be something of a monument also.</i> -Roger Zelazny","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/512-wise-old-guru","name":"Wise Old Guru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar512_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-15T11:32:12-07:00","id":442859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wise Old Guru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/311220-god-kicking-boot-an-exalted-comic-by-wise-old-guru?p=442834#post442834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, how I wish my players looked at mysteries with the eyes you use!<br /> <br /> Storytelling murder mysteries would be much more satisfying.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have two advantages:<br /> <br /> 1) I am observing the story rather than participating in it, which affords me objective distance.<br /> <br /> 2) The story is recorded, so I can read back over a page more than once before analyzing it.<br /> <br /> 3) I am good at logical analysis and driven to understand puzzles.<br /> <br /> ...Three! I have three advantages! [/Spanish Inquisitor]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 03-15-2015, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-22T09:18:19-07:00","id":452757,"title":"","content":"Well, that's ominous.